          "description": "Finally, compare the retrograde loops of Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn side by side. Farther planets produce SMALLER loops because the relative-motion effect shrinks with distance. Use this to predict: retrograde happens near opposition, when Earth passes between the Sun and the outer planet. Tap Finish when done."
        },
